<code>assert \forall int i; 0<=i && i<this.size(); this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i))) => c.contains(this.get(i)));</code>

However, the correct interpretation of the comment is that after `retainAll`, every element in the priority queue should be contained in the collection `c`. Therefore, the correct assert statement should be:

<code>assert \forall int i; 0<=i && i<this.size(); c.contains(this.get(i));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; 0<=i && i<this.size(); c.contains(this.get(i)));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; 0<=i && i<this.size(); this.get(i) != null ==> c.contains(this.get(i));</code>
--------------------
